<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>61.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <decisions>
        <name>Has_Contact</name>
        <label>Has Contact?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Found_Contact</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Brand_Profile_Contact.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Primary_Brand_Contact</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes — Found Contact</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>AF_PrimaryBrandContact__c is a plain manual lookup with no automation writing to it anywhere in the org — live-confirmed zero of the 18 real Opportunities had it populated, which was silently leaving AF_TestDrive__c/Appraisal.AF_Contact__c blank on every Explore-stage auto-create (no valid recipient for the customer confirmation email). Auto-derives it from the Account&apos;s own Brand Profile Contact (RecordType=AF_Brand_Profile) matching the Opportunity&apos;s Brand, whenever it&apos;s blank and both Account and Brand are known. Re-evaluates if Account or Brand changes later, not just at create. Never overwrites a value already set — this only fills in blanks. REAL BUG FIXED 2026-09-01: also re-evaluates on a StageName change (not just Account/Brand) and now runs at triggerOrder 10 (before AF_FL_Opp_CreateExploreSideProcesses&apos;s 40) — previously, an Opportunity whose Account/Brand were set well before its Consider-to-Explore transition (i.e. this flow&apos;s ISNEW()/ISCHANGED(AccountId)/ISCHANGED(AF_Brand__c) conditions never re-fired) would move to Explore with AF_PrimaryBrandContact__c still blank, and the Appraisal/Test Drive auto-create would read that blank value in the same transaction, silently shipping with no Contact. Confirmed live on a real pre-existing Opportunity.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>AF Opp Derive Primary Brand Contact {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Opportunity Derive Primary Brand Contact</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Brand_Profile_Contact</name>
        <label>Get Brand Profile Contact</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>242</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Has_Contact</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>AccountId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AccountId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>RecordTypeId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Brand_Profile_RecordType.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>AF_Brand__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.AF_Brand__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Contact</object>
        <sortField>CreatedDate</sortField>
        <sortOrder>Asc</sortOrder>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Brand_Profile_RecordType</name>
        <label>Get Brand Profile Record Type</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Brand_Profile_Contact</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>SobjectType</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Contact</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>DeveloperName</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>AF_Brand_Profile</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>RecordType</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Set_Primary_Brand_Contact</name>
        <label>Set Primary Brand Contact</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>458</locationY>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>AF_PrimaryBrandContact__c</field>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Brand_Profile_Contact.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputReference>$Record</inputReference>
    </recordUpdates>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Brand_Profile_RecordType</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>AND(
    ISBLANK({!$Record.AF_PrimaryBrandContact__c}),
    NOT(ISBLANK({!$Record.AccountId})),
    NOT(ISBLANK(TEXT({!$Record.AF_Brand__c}))),
    OR(
        ISNEW(),
        ISCHANGED({!$Record.AccountId}),
        ISCHANGED({!$Record.AF_Brand__c}),
        ISCHANGED({!$Record.StageName})
    )
)</filterFormula>
        <object>Opportunity</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
    <triggerOrder>10</triggerOrder>
</Flow>
